{title: Gravel Road Home}

{start_of_verse}
[G]Dust on the dashb[C]oard, sun in my eyes
[G]Radio fading out some[D]where near the county line
[G]Mama's old rosary [C]swings from the glass
[G]Counting the mil[D]e markers goi[G]ng past
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]Take me down the [G]gravel road home
[D]Where the porch light[G]'s always on
[C]I've been running on [G]empty so long
[D]Take me down the grave[G]l road home
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
[G]Fields full of th[C]under, sky full of rain
[G]Every fence post whi[D]spers out my name
[G]Seven hours drivi[C]ng, two cups of coffee cold
[G]Never thought I[D]'d miss it, [G]now I'm getting old
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]Take me down the [G]gravel road home
[D]Where the porch light[G]'s always on
[C]I've been running on [G]empty so long
